## What an Outdoor Movie Night Needs

An outdoor screening is four jobs at once, and each one has a limit worth knowing before you book:

-   **A screen and a projector sized to your audience.** The picture has to be big enough for the last row and bright enough for the light that is left in the sky and around the venue.

-   **Sound that carries.** Dialogue is the part of a film an audience cannot afford to lose, and open air has no walls to hold the sound in.

-   **Power at the right spot.** The projector, the speakers and your playback device all need a reliable supply close to where they stand.

-   **Darkness.** A projected image competes with every other light in the venue, and an outdoor event cannot dim the sun.

We do not run a cinema: we supply the screen, the projector, the sound and the crew who set them up, and you bring the film. For the rest of what we deliver, see [our full audio visual rental range in Malaga](/blog/audio-visual-rental/).

