## Outdoor Movie Screen Rental: Choosing Your Screen and Projector Size

Three of our packages carry a screen and a projector, and one larger screen is available separately:

| Option | Screen | Projector | Package guest capacity | Price (ex VAT) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) with the optional add on | Projector & projection screen, add on | Brightness not published for the add on | Up to 50 | 290 euros base, +50 euros add on |
| [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) | 2x2m projection screen | 3000 lumens | Up to 40 | 295 euros |
| [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) | Front projection screen with a stable stand | 5000 lumens, not laser | Not published | 310 euros |
| Da-Lite screen, separate equipment | 2.30 x 3.00 m, front and rear projection | Quoted with the screen | Not applicable | On request |

All package prices are ex VAT, with 21 percent Spanish VAT added at checkout, and include delivery, setup and teardown. The Da-Lite screen is not included in any package: it is a stand with two screen cloths, built for front and rear projection, and we quote it on request. Tell us the venue and the audience and we confirm what it takes to use it.

How to choose between them comes down to two questions:

-   **How far back does your audience sit?** The farther the last row, the bigger the picture has to be. A 2x2m screen suits a small, close audience. A larger crowd, or a long lawn, points to the 2.30 x 3.00 m screen.

-   **How much light is left?** Lumens measure how bright the image is against the light around it. The 5000 lumen projector is the brighter of our two published tiers, and it is the one to ask about if your venue keeps some light on. Our [projector rental](/blog/projector-rental/) guide explains both lumens tiers in full.

If you want a screen bigger than 2.30 x 3.00 m, that is not in our own inventory. Tell us what you need and we look for the solution with our suppliers, if there is one, with no size or deadline promised.

## Sound for an Outdoor Movie: PA Speakers, Not a Home Cinema System

A film soundtrack is mostly dialogue, and dialogue needs speakers loud and clear enough to reach the back of the audience. That is exactly what a PA system does, and it is what we deliver: PA speakers, tested at your venue before the audience arrives.

-   The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) includes 2 active speakers with stands for up to 50 guests, self run with no technician on site, plus the optional projector and screen add on.

-   The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) is a high end active PA for up to 80 guests with a technician on site.

-   The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) brings professional active speakers for up to 120 guests with a technician for up to 6 hours.

The Wedding Pack and the MICE Pack do not list a projector and projection screen among their inclusions. For a larger crowd, tell us the combination of sound, screen and projector you need and we confirm what is possible.

With no walls to reflect off, open air disperses sound further than a room does, so the speakers are placed to project across the space. Be honest with yourself about what that gives you: a clear, powerful PA, not a surround sound or home cinema system. Our own sound equipment is the PA described above. If your night needs a surround or home cinema system, tell us and we look for the solution with our suppliers, if there is one.

You run the film from your own laptop, tablet or player. On the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) we provide HDMI and USB-C adapters plus audio interfaces to connect your device to our screen and sound system, so the connection is confirmed on arrival rather than solved on the spot.

## Power, Weather and Timing From Dusk to Dark

**Power.** There are no generators or tents in our own inventory. Confirm the power point at your venue when you book, and we size the setup to what is actually available. If the supply genuinely falls short, a generator is something we can try to source from a supplier, with no promise of availability for your date and no promised deadline.

**Ground.** Grass, sand and uneven terraces are normal outdoor venues. Our crew manages cable runs and stand placement for the actual ground surface when we install. A rooftop or a beach venue adds wind exposure, which affects where we place the stands, and the screen is the part of the setup that feels it most. Tell us how open your venue is.

**Weather.** Our crew assesses conditions on site during installation and places the equipment around whatever shelter the venue provides. If rain is a real risk, arrange a covered backup area with your venue in advance. Our [audio visual rental for outdoor events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-outdoor-events/) guide covers villas, terraces, beach clubs and gardens in more detail.

**Timing.** An image is only as good as the dark it is projected into. Ambient light, from the last of the sunset to terrace lights, pool lights or a nearby street lamp, washes out a projected picture. The hour it gets properly dark changes through the year on the Costa del Sol, so plan the start of the film around dusk rather than around the time on the invitation. Ask your venue which of its own lights can be switched off, and use the time before dark for arrivals, food and a short welcome.

