## FAQs

### What size screen do I need for an outdoor movie night, and for how many guests?

It depends on how far back your audience sits more than on the headcount alone. The 2x2m screen on the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) suits a small, close audience, while a larger crowd or a long lawn points to the separate Da-Lite 2.30 x 3.00 m screen, which is quoted on request. Tell us your guest count and the layout of the venue and we confirm what fits. See [Outdoor Movie Screen Rental: Choosing Your Screen and Projector Size](#outdoor-movie-screen-rental-choosing-your-screen-and-projector-size) above.

### Can you set up an outdoor movie screen on grass or sand?

Yes, our crew manages cable runs and stand placement for the actual ground surface at your venue when we install. Beach and rooftop venues add wind exposure, which affects where the stands go, so tell us how open the venue is when you book. See [Power, Weather and Timing From Dusk to Dark](#power-weather-and-timing-from-dusk-to-dark) above.

### What time is it dark enough to start an outdoor movie?

There is no single time, because dusk shifts through the year on the Costa del Sol and your venue may have its own lights. Plan the film to start after the sky has darkened and the venue lights you can control are off, and use the time before for arrivals and food. A brighter projector, such as the 5000 lumen one on the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/), helps when some light stays on, but it does not replace darkness.

### Do you supply the film or the licence to show it?

No. We supply the screen, the projector, the PA sound and the crew who set them up. The film, and the licence to show it to your audience, are the client's responsibility, and licensing is not part of our service.

### Can I play the film from my own laptop or streaming device?

Yes, most screenings run from the host's own laptop, tablet or player. On the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) we provide HDMI and USB-C adapters plus audio interfaces so your device connects to our screen and sound system. Have the film saved on the device so the screening does not depend on the venue's connection.

### What if the venue has no power point or rain is forecast?

Tents and generators are not in our own inventory. Tell us early when your venue has no reliable power or no cover at all, and we can try to source a generator or a tent from a supplier, with no promise of availability for your date or a deadline. For rain, arrange a covered backup area with your venue in advance. See [Power, Weather and Timing From Dusk to Dark](#power-weather-and-timing-from-dusk-to-dark) above.

### How much does an outdoor movie screen and projector rental cost?

The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) is 290 euros base plus a 50 euro add on for the projector and screen. The [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/), with its 2x2m screen and 3000 lumen projector, is 295 euros. The [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/), with its 5000 lumen projector and front projection screen, is 310 euros. All prices are ex VAT, with 21 percent Spanish VAT added at checkout, and include delivery, setup and teardown. The Da-Lite 2.30 x 3.00 m screen is separate equipment and quoted on request.

### Do you rent an inflatable outdoor movie screen?

An inflatable movie screen is not in our own inventory. Tell us what you need and we look for a solution with our suppliers, if there is one, with no availability or deadline promised. It helps to tell us the venue (grass, sand or a terrace, and how exposed it is to wind), your guest count, the size you would like and whether there is a power point. Our own screens are projection screens that come with a projector, and you will find them in [Outdoor Movie Screen Rental: Choosing Your Screen and Projector Size](#outdoor-movie-screen-rental-choosing-your-screen-and-projector-size) above.
